Translation patch: `Sid` and `ComBinlogDumpGtid`

Change:
  - `Sid::tag`: `self.tag.as_ref()` becomes a `match`; `with_interval`: `self.intervals.0.into_owned()` becomes `cow_into_vec(self.intervals.0)` (patch 14).
  - `Sid::len`/`tagged_len`: `saturating::Saturating` arithmetic (`S(a) += S(b)`, `.0`) becomes `u64::saturating_add`; `self.tag.as_ref().map(|t| t.as_str()).unwrap_or("")` becomes a private method `tag_str()` (a `match`).
  - `Sid::serialize_tagged`: `if !tag_str.is_empty() { buf.extend_from_slice(tag_str.as_bytes()) }` becomes the unconditional `extend_from_slice`.
  - `Sid::deserialize_tagged`: the tag moves into a private `Sid::deserialize_tag(tag_len, buf)`; its `io::Error::new(UnexpectedEof, "..")` becomes `misc::io_error_msg`, `std::str::from_utf8(..).map_err(|e| io::Error::new(InvalidData, format!(.., e)))?` becomes `misc::trusted::sid_tag_from_utf8(..)?` (a new function of the module of patch 64 with that body), `buf.0 = &buf.0[tag_len..]` becomes `buf.skip(tag_len)`, and `Tag::new(..).map_err(|e| io::Error::new(InvalidData, e))?` becomes a `match` with `misc::io_error_from` (patch 02).
  - `ComBinlogDumpGtid`: `is_tagged_format` (`iter().any(..)`), the loop of `sid_block_len` (with `Saturating<u32>` becoming `u32::saturating_add`), the serialization loop and the two deserialization loops become recursive free functions (`any_sid_tagged`, `sid_block_len_from`, `serialize_sids_from`, `deserialize_tagged_sids`, `deserialize_untagged_sids`); `serialize` calls `any_sid_tagged` and `sid_block_len_from` directly instead of the two methods, and its `n_sids_header` computation moves into a free function `n_sids_header(tagged, n_sids)`.
Why: Aeneas fails on closures, does not model `Option::as_ref`/`unwrap_or`, `Cow::into_owned`, iterator adaptors or the slice iterator, or the `saturating` crate's operators (a dependency), does not support `dyn` (`io::Error::new`) or `format!`, and fails on loops over slices of `Sid` (which hold borrows) and on joins after an `if` in `serialize_tagged`/`serialize`, and on calling the `&self` methods from `serialize` ("Unreachable").
Behaviour: Identical. `saturating` 0.1.0 defines `Saturating(a) + Saturating(b)` as `Saturating(a.saturating_add(b))` and `+=` as `*self = *self + other`. Appending an empty slice is a no-op. `skip(n)` is `self.0 = &self.0[n..]`. The recursion visits the sids in order and counts `n_sids` iterations, with the same early `Err` returns; `Vec::with_capacity(n_sids as usize)` is still allocated before the loop. The recursion uses stack proportional to the number of sids.

